  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_e8cdbe111236476f865981a0cf9752d4",
      "statement": "PRSP-HMS-3.4 is Crestline National Bank's RESTRICTED - FINANCIAL CRIMES design document (v3.4, Approved, last reviewed 2026-06-24) owned by Financial Crimes Technology (Daniel Kowalski / Grace Mensah), approved by Victor Petrov and reviewed by FCC Policy & Advisory, that defines the Hold Management Service's hold lifecycle, hold reason taxonomy, controls, interfaces and data-handling rules.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L1-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c993e953884a8fb6f99c08592f09ba55f185b848f53c08273d6c9060dda15d68:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b2ff727b9e44e8ab64969d3c5b44335",
      "statement": "The Hold Management Service (HMS) is the system of record for holds on outbound payments and is one of three components of the Payment Risk & Screening Platform (PRSP), alongside Sentinel Fraud Scoring (vendor model M-FCT-0021) and SanctionScreen; HMS work queues surface to Payment Operations and the FIU via the Investigations Workbench (IWB).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L24-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f6fb690120df161b152daf802cd9a5d75abcf329a7d1f3edc5375f7506369281:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_11c37188434c4070b62d310168ec1e65",
      "statement": "A hold progresses through the states OPEN, IN_REVIEW, ESCALATED, RELEASED, REJECTED, BLOCKED, and EXPIRED; RELEASED/REJECTED occur via maker-checker disposition, BLOCKED moves funds to a blocked account reported to OFAC within 10 business days (31 CFR 501.603), and EXPIRED auto-cancels holds HRC-01/02/05 after the client response window.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L28-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3289fc66d676d11e5fff1066c372a6656b4e757edd15a85e02a56238b140704d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c3521c6653044588da5456260b7ce00",
      "statement": "HMS defines twelve Hold Reason Codes (HRC-01 through HRC-12), each with a disclosure tier (P/C/G/R per POL-FCC-014) and an observed share of hold volume; HRC-07 FRAUD_MODEL_HIGH, HRC-08 ATO_SUSPECT, HRC-09 SANCTIONS_REVIEW, HRC-10 AML_REVIEW and HRC-11 LEGAL_HOLD are tier R, HRC-12 OPS_MANUAL_REVIEW is tier G, HRC-04 CUTOFF_WAREHOUSED is tier P, and the remainder are tier C.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L40-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:95994f4b2ec5fe0fe6be45d147c50e2ee5bbeb69c461f0b31cdeef665eb58d0b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3497fa64cd274b52b379e42d8887b1c8",
      "statement": "Observed HMS volume is approximately 410 holds per business day (2.6% of outbound wires), with median time-to-disposition of roughly 47 minutes for HRC-01, 2h10m for HRC-02, 1h35m for HRC-07, 3h20m for HRC-09, and 1-5 business days for HRC-10.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L70-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47b065ca889c7e8d8ae3d05a08852b2cc3efd2ea7d7f5925d53c5793979716de:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5e69a611f3af4d55a9aacbb57fb707b8",
      "statement": "HMS hold `description` and `analystNotes` fields are classified Restricted and are generated from rule templates that embed HRC mnemonics and investigative context (e.g. fraud score, sanctions match confidence); a legacy HMS-to-PPH sync feeds the PPH v1 `holdReasonDesc` field, predates ADR-PAY-021, and remains active only as a time-boxed v1 backward-compatibility exception tracked as open risk FCT-2004.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L72-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:417834ca8b8dea07e395042dee88b5845b075b2b18891a5ae4c83821b5f2d613:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af742b3710244ed194d2304fa4b06836",
      "statement": "The Kafka topic risk.hold.events.v1 is restricted to FCT and Payment Operations tooling and channel applications are not authorized consumers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L78-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d92e1e18563acf9ee8645407a3f2d9c07da41488977ab09530608cb38aad7694:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_752b8aa991154bdd8ef58e91658154ed",
      "statement": "HMS exposes EP-HMS-01 (GET /prsp/hms/v1/holds?paymentId=, returning hrcCode/category/description/analystNotes/slaDueTs to IWB and PPH's legacy sync), EP-HMS-02 (POST /prsp/hms/v1/holds/{holdId}/disposition, IWB-only, requiring the HOLD_RELEASER role under maker-checker control CTRL-PAY-012), and EV-HMS-01 (the restricted risk.hold.events.v1 topic); no client-facing interface currently exists, and proposal FCT-1893 to add a client-view facade was deprioritized in 2025-Q3.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L80-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2106f98fbd574b8cd510cc5d07e5757a1f9796e1bc661d226e4ad0ba71f20559:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cb930ce06d1c49b9910f029109879696",
      "statement": "HMS defines four disposition controls: CTRL-PAY-012 (maker-checker for release/reject by HOLD_RELEASER role), CTRL-PAY-018 (out-of-band phone callback verification for HRC-02, not satisfiable via the initiating channel), CTRL-PAY-031 (since 2026-06, following the FCT-1951 pilot, HRC-01-only digital attestation with step-up authentication, capped at $5,000,000 above which Wire Room release is required), and CTRL-PAY-040 (no client-facing release-time estimate for tier G or R holds).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L90-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e2534c9ba23d6c0d8aad78f1b4e1c584e504adade490ac3ee8a66fdfaf9967b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1ad5ff293c0a4c369654fb0d0c07ad3c",
      "statement": "For sanctions-related blocks or rejects, Sanctions Operations (not channels) notifies the client in writing per the Sanctions Operations Procedure and reports to OFAC under 31 CFR 501.603 (blocked) or 501.604 (rejected); channels must never communicate screening outcomes.",
      "evidence": [
